@page "/docs/cli/crud"

@* izzy add crud <Model> (catalog/crud in src/IzzyBlazor.Cli): the grid page it writes, how it reads the model,
   the store, the options, and Pro's --mode pages (artifacts/izzyblazor-crud-design.md). *@

<ArticlePage Section="cli" Slug="crud">
    <Lead>
        <Code>izzy add crud</Code> creates a <Anchor Href="docs/components/data-grid">DataGrid</Anchor> page to display,
        add, edit and delete a model's records, for internal tools and admin screens. Name a class from your app; izzy
        reads it from the source, so the app doesn't have to build first.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Add the page</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="bash">izzy add crud Customer</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            This creates a page at <Code>/customers</Code>. The grid on it can search, sort and page the customers. Add and
            Edit open a dialog that checks the form against the model's attributes, and Delete asks before it deletes.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            The toolbar also has Columns and Export. Columns lets each person choose which columns to show, and remembers
            the choice in a cookie. Export downloads the rows as an Excel file, from an endpoint in
            <Code>Data/CustomerExport.cs</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            It works on static pages and on interactive pages. When the app has accounts, the user must sign in to open it.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Where the records are kept</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The page loads and saves records through an <Code>ICustomerStore</Code>. If one of your DbContexts has a
            <Code>DbSet&lt;Customer&gt;</Code>, the store uses it. Otherwise the records are kept in memory until the app
            stops. To choose for yourself, set <Code>--store</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Labels and fields</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Each field's label comes from <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code>, or from the property's name split into words. A
            column's title comes from <Code>ShortName</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Some properties don't get a field: a key the database creates, read-only properties and computed ones. Related
            records, such as a customer's orders, aren't included either. izzy lists each property it leaves out.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            A key people type in, such as an invoice number, needs the Pro pages. They ask for it when adding a record and
            show it read-only when editing.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Options</Heading>
        <Table Items="CrudOptions" Caption="izzy add crud options" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Option" Width="Length.Rem(14)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="What it does">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>

        <Heading Level="2">A page for each task, with Pro</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The grid page does everything in one place and edits in a dialog. With IzzyBlazor Pro, <Code>--mode pages</Code>
            creates separate pages instead: a list with filters, a details page for each customer, and a form page that
            lists its errors at the top. Records with many fields have more room on pages of their own.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">After the model changes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Run the command again with <Code>--diff</Code> to see what would change. Then run it with
            <Code>--overwrite</Code> to update the files. See <Anchor Href="docs/cli/changes">Previewing changes</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Row(string Name, string Text);

    private static readonly Row[] CrudOptions =
    [
        new("--mode pages", "Pro. Creates separate pages to list, show and edit the records, for records with many fields. Without it, izzy creates one grid page that edits in a dialog."),
        new("--name <Plural>", "Sets the folder, the page names and the page title. Defaults to the model's plural, such as Customers."),
        new("--singular <words>", "Sets what one record is called on the page, when it isn't the class name. For example, --singular \"team member\" for a Member class. To set the plural, use --plural."),
        new("--route <path>", "Sets the page's URL. Defaults to the name in kebab case, such as customers."),
        new("--store ef|memory", "Sets where the records are kept. ef needs a DbSet of the model. When two DbContexts have one, choose with --context."),
        new("--authorize", "Lets only signed-in people open the page. On by default when the app has accounts."),
    ];
}
